---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { EXPERIMENTS } from '../../lib/experiments/catalog';
import { loadExperiment } from '../../lib/experiments/load';
import { verdict } from '../../lib/experiments/data';
import { pageHref } from '../../lib/paths';
const releases=await Promise.all(EXPERIMENTS.map(def=>loadExperiment(def)));
---
<BaseLayout evidenceOnly title="Experiments" description="Registered ChronoRoute experiments, with manifested results, confidence intervals and cases where the protocol loses.">
 <header class="page-hero container"><p class="eyebrow">Results</p><h1>Experiments</h1><p class="lede">Questions, registered hypotheses and results from the reviewed experiment releases. Every chart and table reads the same verified summary CSV offered for download.</p></header>
 <section class="section section--flush"><div class="container prose"><h2>What these results describe</h2><p>Network outcomes are MODELLED; comparison statistics and size accounting are DERIVED. C5 orbital inputs are REAL public data. C2 orbits and positions are MODELLED. Starlink’s operational routing is UNKNOWN; Starlink does not use T-CRH.</p><p>Intervals are taken from the result files. Exact correctness and byte-accounting checks have no sampling interval. These experiments do not establish a universal winner; each verdict below says whether the registered hypothesis is supported, not supported or mixed, and each experiment page lists the caveats behind it.</p></div></section>
 <section class="section"><div class="container"><h2>Registered experiments</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Reviewed releases; no pilot or failed attempt is selected automatically.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Experiment</th><th scope="col">Question</th><th scope="col">Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody>{releases.map(data=><tr><th scope="row"><a href={pageHref(`experiments/${data.definition.slug}`)}>{data.definition.slug.toUpperCase()}: {data.definition.title}</a></th><td>{data.definition.question}</td><td>{verdict(data.definition,data.rows,data.contrasts?.rows??null).summary}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
